<Base title="About — Vansh"><section class="shell page-section about-page"><div class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE NOTEBOOK</div><h1 class="page-title">Hi, I’m Vansh<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p class="about-lead">A mechanical engineering student with an aerospace concentration, a fascination with flight, and a habit of asking how things work.</p><div class="about-columns"><div class="prose"><h2>Engineering, with curiosity.</h2><p>I’m studying at Hofstra University and serve as co-president of our AIAA chapter. I’m interested in aircraft design, rocketry, simulation, and the practical work of turning an idea into something you can test.</p><p>This site is a place to document what I’m learning and building: technical projects, explanations, experiments, and the occasional exploration of new technology.</p><h2>What you’ll find here</h2><p>Work on aerospace questions, computational tools, and open technology. I want to make the reasoning visible, including assumptions, limitations, and the places where a model stops being useful.</p><h2>Let’s connect</h2><p>{site.email ? <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Send me an email ↗</a> : 'Contact links will appear here once I add them.'}</p>{site.github&&<p><a href={site.github}>GitHub ↗</a></p>}{site.linkedin&&<p><a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a></p>}</div><aside class="profile-panel"><div class="eyebrow">CURRENT INTERESTS</div><ul><li>Blended-wing-body aircraft</li><li>Flight mechanics & performance</li><li>Rocket trajectory simulation</li><li>Scientific computing</li><li>Linux & open-source tools</li></ul><div class="profile-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Learning. Building. Iterating.</div></aside></div></section></Base>
